+Arbitrary post-commit maintenance tasks can also be registered through the generic `maintenance(...)` method, which may be called multiple times:
+
+```java
+IcebergSink.forRowData(dataStream)
+    .table(table)
+    .tableLoader(tableLoader)
+    .maintenance(RewriteDataFiles.builder()
+        .scheduleOnDataFileCount(20))
+    .maintenance(ExpireSnapshots.builder()
+        .retainLast(5))
+    .maintenance(DeleteOrphanFiles.builder()
+        .minAge(Duration.ofDays(3)))
+    .append();
+```
+
 ##### Config
 
 All maintenance tasks are configured through string properties:
@@ -421,6 +436,9 @@ These keys are used in SQL (SET or table WITH options) or via `IcebergSink.Build
 | `flink-maintenance.expire-snapshots.enabled` | Enable expire snapshots | `false` |
 | `flink-maintenance.delete-orphan-files.enabled` | Enable delete orphan files | `false` |
 
+!!! note
+    The legacy key `compaction-enabled` is deprecated in favor of `flink-maintenance.rewrite.enabled` and is still accepted as an alias.
